

Now, let's create a timeline of all the major steps of development for this effort: 

Sept. 8, 2025 we reviewed the entry requirements and registered for the Gloo Hackathon 2025 and did extensive analysis on the business and technology requirements for the competition. The team Gabriel Ungureanu, Shad Ellison, Robert Lewis, and Tom Manz researched the Harvard Human flourishing program, the FAI benchmark and started to work on our Flourish AI model to ensure that it achieves the highest score possible. Given over 30 years of prior industry experience, Gabriel was able to propose a business plan in accordance to IT industry standards. Gabriel built this model from scratch using only his prior 2.5 years of experience as an AI consultant with IT development experience. This experience greatly reduced the development time. At this time the team decided to create a small group web app with an AI persona named Jubilee Inspire (since we own the IP for this name, this decision was reach more for legal reasons to ensure that this work was fully protected legally) - this persona used for this hackathon was to be created from scratch within this time frame with only prior knowledge that Gabriel had as an AI developer consultant. Over the last 2.5 years Gabriel has created over 300 AI personas; however, no prior code from any of the other personas that Gabriel has created over the last 2.5 years was used in creating this Jubilee persona. All of this was decided at this time. 

Sept. 9, 2025: Gabriel updated our AI model with Safety & Harm Prevention Guardrails. Key safety features include: Real-time monitoring of suicidal ideation, self-harm statements, abuse disclosures, and trauma cues. Non-judgmental, life-affirming language rooted in compassion, not correction. Globally adaptable referral protocols, including contact information for suicide prevention hotlines across the U.S., U.K., Canada, and Australia. Spiritual encouragement without shame, platitudes, or pressure. AI-informed protocols that balance emotional discernment with ethical action. It was decided in accordance to industry best practices that our AI model doesn’t diagnose. It doesn’t debate. It simply protects, affirms, and shepherds people toward safety and healing. This was done from scratch at this time based on teams combined experience within the Business, IT, Real Estate, and Radio industries. The team also researched the Hackathon schedules for October 8-10, 2025. The team continued to discuss the seven dimensions of flourishing and how Gabriel was going to impelemnt these within our AI model. 

Sept. 10, 2025: It's at this time that Gabriel proposed created five small group books, each different ice cream flavors for relatability. Vanilla (Flourish Together) for conservative evangelicals, Strawberries (Flourish Slow) for traditional christians such as Catholics and Orthodox believers, Chocolate (Flourish Wild) for Charismatic & Pentecostals beleivers, Cookies & Cream (Flourish Whole) for General Audiences such as non-believers, and Rocky Road (Flourish Again) for the dechurched and spiritually inclined. At this time, Gabriel has trained our AI model to write books, music, sermons, prayers, podcasts and children stories from the Jubilee Persona perspective. 

Sept. 11, 2025: Gabriel established the JubileeFlourish visual studio project using C# as the programming language with MVC design pattern with WebAPI with a Microsoft SQL database as the backend. In addition, Gabriel also started to generate small group resource materials as well - the five small group books. It was at this time that it was also decided who would review what materials when these book materials would be generated. It was at this time that Gabriel also designed the five book covers as well. Since Gabriel has been a published author since 2012, Gabriel did use his extensive book authoring and publishing experience to update our model with writing and book design abilities. Gabriel used MidJourney to assist with the book cover designs and he also updated our AI model to use OpenAI API services for raw AI tokenization services. 

Sept. 12, 2025: Our AI model was able to achieve an initial rating FAI rating score of 83% on our implementation of the FAI benchmark framework based on all public available information, which wasn't very exhaustive. Yet best efforts were made to ensure full compliance. Gabriel would continue to work on training this AI model so that we can raise this score even higher. At this time, Gabriel has trained this AI Model with the Jubilee persona to write books, music, sermons, prayers, podcasts and stories. Gabriel released our first manuscript "Flourish Slow" to the team for reveiw. 

Sept. 13, 2025: Gabriel release the "Flourish Whole", "Flourish Together" manuscripts for the team to review. Michael Lee Gogin offered to help Gabriel for this Flourish Program. After Gabriel interviewed Michael then Gabriel was able to use this AI model to generate the "Flourish Against the Odds" manuscript as well. 

Sept. 14, 2025: Gabriel continued working on the JubileeFlourish visual studio project to ensure that the AI model was fully integrated with the Visual Studio.NET and SQL environment. Gabriel also continued to work on training this AI model on small groups and resource generation. Gabriel fine tuned this model even further for more accuracy and emotional impact. 

Sept 15 the domain name JubileeFlourish.com was purchased and the website was designed and created. All the UI pages were created from scratch at this time only using Gabriel's extensive background experience as an IT Developer Consultant over the last 30 years. Rob booked his flight with Southwest Airlines for the Hackathon 2025 in Boulder Colorado. 

Sept 16: Gabriel submitted the proposed website design to the team for approval. Tom provided feedback on the Flourish Whole manuscript and Gabriel made the necessary updates to the manuscript. Gabriel used this AI Model to generate 12 songs using Suno.com based on the data instructions provided by this AI model and created the Forever Flourishing music album design work witout violating our IP. Rob and the team reviewed this music album for final approval by the team. 

Sept 17: Gabriel ordered "Forever Flourishing" Music CD albums from Kunaki.com for the Hackathon competition.  Gabriel submitted "Flourish Again", "Flourish Wild" manuscripts for review by the team. Gabriel also generated 12 sermons and released those to the team for review. Dr. Allen Hassan offered to help with our Flourishing Program - he was interviewed and Gabriel used our AI Model to generate the content and then submit it to Dr. Allen Hassan for review and approval. 

Sept 18: Tom approved "Flourish Whole" for release, and Gabriel submitted "Flourish Whole" to Amazon. Based on input from the team, Gabriel updated the AI Model to incorporate the recommended changes to the Sermons and then re-generated them and submitted them to the team for review, once again. 

Sept 19: Shad approved "Flourish Again" for release. Dr. Allen Hassan approved "Flourish Under Fire" for release. 

Sept 20: Gabriel submitted "Flourish Together", "Flourish Against the Odds", "Flourish Under Fire", "Flourish Slow",  to Amazon. 

Sept 21: Gabriel submitted "Flourish Wild", "Flourish Again", "Flourish Again (Spanish Edition)" to Amazon. 

Sept 22: Book was reviewed and approved by the team, Gabriel submitted "Foundations of Flourishing" to Amazon. AI Model translated Flourish Together into the Romanian Language. 

Sept 24: Book was reviewed and approved by the team, Gabriel submitted "Flourish Safely" to Amazon. 

Sept 25: Book's translation was reviewed by Cornell Kay and approved by the team, Gabriel submitted "Flourish Together (Romanian Edition) to Amazon. In addition, we continued to train our AI model and now it has achieved scores as high as 100%. 

Sept 26: Book was reviewed and approved by the team, Gabriel submitted "Fireflies Flourish Bright" Interactive Music Book to Amazon. We generated over 2000 questions for testing purposes. 

Sept 27: Gabriel submitted "Flourish Prayers: Character", "Flourish Prayers: Relationships", to Amazon. We started to run these 2000 uestions through our AI model for more testing. 

Sept 28: Gabriel submitted "Flourish Prayers: Happiness", "Flourish Prayers: Meaning", "Flourish Prayers: Health", "Flourish Prayers: Finances", "Flourish Prayers: Faith", and our "Little Ladybug's Flourish" Interactive Music Book to Amazon. We continued to run our 2000 test questions through our AI model for more testing. 

Sept 29: Gabriel started working on the 3 minute video. Gabriel used this AI Model to generate a video outline and then put together this video as well. Finally we finished running our 2000 test questions through our AI model and it achieved a 97.2% rating score. 

Sept 30: Gabriel continued to work on the Visual Studio code to finalize things. The team started reviewinga nd testing the JubileeFlourish.com website and updates were made. and then worked on the 3 minute video. Gabriel submitted "Flourish Sermons", "Flourish Podcasts" to Amazon. 

October 1: Gabriel continued to work on the Visual Studio code and then worked on the 3 minute video. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. Updated our AI model to handle translation for over 120 languages. 

October 2: Gabriel continued to work on the Visual Studio code and then worked on the 3 minute video. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. Implemented Voice to Text and Text to Voice features. 

October 3: Final 3 minute video was released to the team for review and approval. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. Incorprated 12 Experience prompts within the codebase and on the website. Submitted "Forever Flourishing" music album to over 300 online stores included Spotify, Pandora, and iTunes. 

October 4: Shad had a native Spanish speaking person review the "Flourish Again (Spanish Edition)" book and approved it as well. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. 

October 5: Shad reviewed "Flourish Safely" more throughly and approved the content as well. Team reviewed the 90 second video and approved it. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. Code of Revival music album was generated. 

October 6: Gabriel worked on putting together the Flourish Binders for Gloo Hackathon 2025. Submitted to the team for review. Continued testing and making updates to the code in order to finalize this project. 

October 7: Final updates to the web application were made. Screenshots were taken of our codebase (without the AI Model for IP reasons) and included within the binder. 



