Christine: Tell Gabriel that using the "-" is a clear indication of using an AI tool because people rarely use that in writing

Gabriel: I’ve been using hyphens since high school and I also like to use “…” as well. But, I suppose that I’m different like that. 

However, there’s a urban legend going around that only AI uses hyphens-which is not true. 

If you look it up, you’ll discover that 50% to 80% of human written prose works use the hyphen as a dash to break up thoughts in fresh and exciting ways. Which is how I have used it all these years. 

That’s approximately 50 million people that currently use hyphens in their writings; however, some reporter came out and said that only AI uses hyphens (I suppose that they don’t use hyphens themselves) and that’s how you can tell it has been written by AI and somehow everybody now believes this without checking the facts. 

Now, most scientific writings don’t use the hyphen as much, which is an indication of left brain writing. Any way - I had to explain this several times to people already. Besides, AI learned to use hyphens from all the human data that has hyphens in it. 

Something to think about. 

